dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.animation.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.animation
start body
framing record

# animation wave (following the flow pilot's proven template): REAL binary pack frame,
# replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s old
# `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly, via the PROVEN
# bare `segment` form, not the braced form) are genuinely, fully described. Past that, `timelines`
# (and its nested `channels`/`keyframes`) is a HOMOGENEOUS but variable-length repeated record,
# further embedding two data-carrying tagged unions (`AnimTargetProperty`/`AnimValue`) — the
# `protocol-array-of-records` gap (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N
# from a count field", for an untagged homogeneous record): modeled as one opaque trailing
# `payload` chain, the same honest boundary every prior semio wave's own nested/recursive payload
# uses. The real Rust `encode_animation_snapshot_binary`/`decode_animation_snapshot_binary` stays
# genuinely, fully structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real `f64` LE fields, a
# real per-variant tag byte for `AnimTargetProperty`/`AnimInterpolation`/`AnimValue`) — round-trip
# tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops here.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
